From 9cdd022ce2fc6f56b52a6e90aa8083c2d5de02e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Veremeev <6252647+BarabashkaD@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:40:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rk86_16: vt57 SI request state before S0 (Fig. 6 note 1;
 review M9, for decision)

The theta-down that sees a DRQ keeps the 8257 in SI with HRQ set at the next
theta-up; S0 follows one theta-down later ([C78] 12-104 Fig. 6 note 1, the
12-110 waveform). The first HLDA sample moves from 9 to 18 ce16 after the
DRQ sample; with the 8080 every pin edge is unchanged (S1 27 after the
sample, HRQ up 4 after it).

tb_vt57_func check 20 'si hrq': HLDA held high before DRQ0, HRQ 4 and S1
18 after the DRQ sample. New fault vt57f_si_to_s0_at_sample (S0 at the
sample). Regenerated for the new context: vt57_one_edge, vt57_s0_no_hlda
(now 'latency 18'), vt57_hrq_late (the extra sample in req),
vt57f_s0_no_return, vt57f_autoload_early.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
